  "id": "eoagritwin-lstsdd",
  "stac_version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Annual crop-specific Land Surface Temperature Stress Degree Days (LSTSDDs; Schreier et al. 2026, in review) for maize, potato, sugar beet, winter rapeseed and winter wheat over Germany for the years 2017 to 2024, produced in the EOAgriTwin project. LSTSDDs quantify the cumulative heat exposure of a crop during its growing season: daily Sentinel-3 SLSTR land surface temperature is accumulated within crop-specific phenological phases derived from DWD phenological observations (DWD 2026) and restricted to the pixels of each crop according to the national crop type maps of Blickensdoerfer et al. (2022) and Schwieder et al. (2022). The product is provided as one Zarr data cube per crop (time x latitude x longitude, one layer per year) on a 0.01 degree grid (EPSG:4326), in degree Celsius days. Pixels without the respective crop are set to NaN.",
